|CKBRanger|000

|CK0Rangers are self-sufficient wilderness specialists who combine tracking,
terrain knowledge, crafting, archery, close combat, camps, concealment, nature
magic, and animal companions.|000

|CKBHow it plays|000
|CK0A Ranger chooses primary and secondary terrain, favored quarry, and a
personal skill tree. Terrain changes damage, costs, recovery, and available
companions. Survival work turns wood, hide, ore, herbs, and trophies into tools,
weapons, ammunition, salves, poisons, and camps.|000

|CKBCore skills|000
|CK0survey and rtrack read the land, forage and harvest gather supplies, camp
creates a field base, attract finds a companion, conceal and ambush prepare an
opening, quickshot and heartshot support archery, and strike, gash, impale,
winterbite, and naturestrike cover close combat and magic.|000

|CKBBest fit|000
|CK0Choose Ranger if you enjoy preparation, exploration, crafting, pets, and
adapting to terrain. It offers exceptional breadth, but expects more fieldwork
and planning than a purely martial guild.|000

|CK0After joining, use |CKBranhelp general|CK0, |CKBskilltree|CK0,
|CKBsurvey|CK0, and |CKBrscore|CK0 for the full field guide.|000

